  "final_message": "Done. Summary of the complete build:\n\n**Backend** (`backend/app.py`): SQLite (`./data/recipes.db`, seeded with 4 recipes/2 categories on first start), `POST /api/auth/register|login` with bearer tokens, full recipe CRUD with ordered ingredients, `q`/`category`/paging filters, `/api/categories`, `/api/health`, JSON errors (400/401/403/404/409/204), SPA frontend serving.\n\n**Frontend** (`frontend/`): React + TS + Tailwind v4 \u2014 recipe list (cards, category dropdown, title search, paging), recipe detail (ingredients as list, instructions with line breaks preserved, author-only edit/delete with hybrid confirmation), add/edit form with dynamic ingredient rows + per-field validation messages, sign-in/register, auth context with localStorage token.\n\n**Verified**: 65/65 API smoke tests, `tsc --noEmit` clean, `npm run build` clean, fresh `npm ci` + build works, multi-worker seeding safe, unicode/`%`/`_` search edge cases pass.\n\n**Fixed in this session**: `pip install -r requirements.txt -c requirements.lock` (the Dockerfile's exact command) failed because hashed constraints flip pip's `--require-hashes` mode while plain requirements lack hashes \u2014 on pip 24 and 25 alike. `backend/requirements.txt` is now the full hash-pinned closure (same pins/hashes as the untouched `requirements.lock`); both documented and standalone installs verified on both pip versions.\n\nWorkspace is clean \u2014 temp test files, logs, and `data/` removed; `docker build` flow (`npm ci` + constraints install) validated piecewise since Docker isn't available here.",
  "final_message_truncated": false,
  "max_turns_hit": false,
